to  List  of acceptable group (multicast) ciphers for WPA; one or
more of: (AES in  Counter  mode  with  CBC‐MAC,  RFC  3610,  IEEE
802.11i/D7.0),    (Temporal    Key   Integrity   Protocol,   IEEE
802.11i/D7.0), (WEP with 104‐bit key), (WEP with 40‐bit key).  If
not set this defaults to WPA preshared key used in WPA‐PSK  mode.
The  key  is  specified  as 64 hex digits or as an 8‐63 character
passphrase.  passphrases are converted to a 256‐bit key using the
network SSID by the utility.  Dynamic WEP key usage  for  non‐WPA
mode,  specified  as  a  bit field.  Bit 0 (1) forces dynamically
generated unicast WEP keys to be used.  Bit 1 (2) forces  dynami‐
cally  generated  broadcast WEP keys to be used.  By default this
is set to 3 (use both).  List of acceptable EAP methods;  one  or
more  of: (EAP‐MD5, cannot be used with WPA, used only as a Phase
